  This exception covers your programs. It does NOT extend to the Yon
  compiler, frontend, MLIR dialect, toolchain, or to the runtime
  library itself: any modified version of those remains governed by
  the full AGPLv3, including its network-use provision.

  If you modify this runtime library, you may extend this exception to
  your version, but you are not obliged to do so. If you do not wish
  to, delete this exception statement from your version.

In plain words: programs you write in Yon are yours, under any license
you like. Yon itself — the compiler and this runtime — stays free, and
anyone improving or serving it must share those improvements.

This exception follows the established pattern of the GCC Runtime
Library Exception and the GNU Classpath Exception.
